-- Coordinator-owned Serre algebra and finite exactness.
-- Definitions open only their displayed quotient/type carriers and equations.
-- Finite products use common denominator and equality-exponent bounds.
-- Cokernel structure descends the existing Cech quotient; native exactness
-- then proves its localisation comparison. Equalisers use the difference
-- kernel and the named homotopy comparison, never a new kernel construction.
-- No quotient, function-extensionality or localisation proof is reopened.
